<item>
            <title>[LU-20783] llite: ignore &quot;nolock&quot; mount option, remove LL_IOC_SETFLAGS</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20783</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14838&quot; title=&quot;Remove old lockless code: Truncate &amp;amp; contention based lockless i/o&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-14838&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14838&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; removed lockless truncate, and the client side of contention-based lockless buffered I/O. Two ways to request lockless I/O explicitly are still in master, and both reach buffered I/O.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. The &lt;tt&gt;nolock&lt;/tt&gt; mount option (&lt;tt&gt;LL_SBI_NOLCK&lt;/tt&gt;)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The flag comment says &quot;DLM locking disabled directio-only&quot;, but nothing enforces that. With the option set, &lt;tt&gt;ll_file_nolock()&lt;/tt&gt; is true for every file. &lt;tt&gt;ll_io_init()&lt;/tt&gt; then sets &lt;tt&gt;ci_lockreq = CILR_NEVER&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;ci_no_srvlock = 1&lt;/tt&gt;, and &lt;tt&gt;vvp_io_rw_lock()&lt;/tt&gt; passes &lt;tt&gt;CEF_NEVER&lt;/tt&gt;, for buffered I/O as well as direct I/O. A buffered write goes through &lt;tt&gt;osc_io_commit_async()&lt;/tt&gt; into the page cache with no client DLM lock and no server-side lock. Only mmap and a few other operations refuse &lt;tt&gt;nolock&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. &lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_SETFLAGS&lt;/tt&gt; with &lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_IGNORE_LOCK&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The ioctl refuses &lt;tt&gt;IGNORE_LOCK&lt;/tt&gt; on a file not opened &lt;tt&gt;O_DIRECT&lt;/tt&gt;, but it checks only when the flag is set. llite has no &lt;tt&gt;check_flags()&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;fcntl(F_SETFL)&lt;/tt&gt; can clear &lt;tt&gt;O_DIRECT&lt;/tt&gt; afterwards. Later buffered I/O on that file descriptor is then lockless in the same way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both were found by reading the code; neither has been reproduced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lockless buffered I/O cannot be kept consistent across clients, for the reasons given in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14838&quot; title=&quot;Remove old lockless code: Truncate &amp;amp; contention based lockless i/o&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-14838&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14838&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. It also breaks an assumption elsewhere. Before lock replay, the no-wait LRU cancel selects only locks with no dirty or writeback pages under them (see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20157&quot; title=&quot;deadlock between recovery and IO&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20157&quot;&gt;LU-20157&lt;/a&gt;). A lockless writer can dirty pages under such a lock without ever touching the lock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For direct I/O these interfaces add nothing useful. Direct I/O is already lockless on the client by default, and these interfaces also drop the server-side lock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Proposed change&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Stop honouring the &lt;tt&gt;nolock&lt;/tt&gt; mount option. Keep accepting it, so that existing fstab entries still mount, but print a warning that it is ignored and mount with normal locking.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Remove the &lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_SETFLAGS&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_CLRFLAGS&lt;/tt&gt; handling, and keep both ioctl numbers reserved in &lt;tt&gt;lustre_user.h&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_IGNORE_LOCK&lt;/tt&gt; is the only flag a caller can usefully set through them:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_GROUP_LOCKED&lt;/tt&gt; is refused.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_READAHEA&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_LOCKED_DIRECTIO&lt;/tt&gt; are not referenced anywhere in the tree.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;LL_FILE_FLOCK_WARNING&lt;/tt&gt; is internal state.&lt;br/&gt;
Nothing in-tree (&lt;tt&gt;lfs&lt;/tt&gt;, liblustreapi, the test suite) calls either ioctl.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Remove &lt;tt&gt;ll_file_nolock()&lt;/tt&gt;. Once &lt;tt&gt;CILR_NEVER&lt;/tt&gt; is gone, also remove any lockless handling on the buffered write path that becomes unreachable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
